WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:03.430
<i>Kaitobingu da</i>! Kaito!

00:00:03.790 --> 00:00:06.670
Brother's eyes are trying to answer Yuma.

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:09.110
I don't know, what is waiting for me ahead,

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:12.130
but I will open up my own path!

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:13.590
My own Duel!

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.520
Then, come on, Kaito!

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:21.750
You will regret waking up the sleeping lion.

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:23.290
That's what I want!

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:24.880
My turn.

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:27.080
Draw!

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:30.910
I activate the magic card Cards of Adversity.

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.890
When there is no monster on my field,

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:37.060
and there are special summoned monsters on the opponent's field,

00:00:37.810 --> 00:00:40.840
I can draw 2 cards.

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:46.030
The I activate the magic card Accel Light.

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:49.830
If there are no monsters on my field,

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:53.180
Instead of normal summoning this turn,

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:59.010
from my deck, I can special summon
one LV 4 Light Warrior-type monster.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:02.380
I special summon Day Breaker!

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:11.070
Day Braker... Yuma, be careful.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:11.650
Sure!

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:14.830
When a Day Breaker has been special summoned,

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:18.840
I can special summon another Day Breaker from my hand.

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:24.970
I overlay my 2 LV 4 Day Breaker.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:30.200
With these 2 monsters, I build the overlay network.

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:31.950
Xyz summon!

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:37.800
Come forth, Photon Knight Paladius!

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.060
There it is.

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:41.460
Be ready, it's coming!

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:44.400
The effect of Photon Knight Paladius activates!

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:48.070
Once per turn, by detaching one overlay unit,

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:53.780
Until the end of the battle, the ATK of 1 Xyz-monster on the opponents field is changed to Zero,

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:57.740
also the effects of all other cards than Paladius are negated.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:02.000
This means as Hope's effects are gone...

00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:05.310
That's right, even if it is a Numbers, it can be destroyed.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:07.730
Do it, Paladius!

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:09.000
Photon Dividing!

00:02:17.890 --> 00:02:19.810
With this I end my turn.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.140
As to be expected from Kaito.

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:31.510
Sure, but if it weren't like that, it wouldn't be interesting.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:34.290
It's a good wall for the <i>Kattobingu</i>!

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:38.240
Unfortunately, you won't bear it down, it's not a brittle wall.

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:41.610
If that's the case, I'll bear it down anyway!

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:48.250
<i>Advance, advance, beyond the limits of your strength</i>

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:53.800
<i>Come along with me and burn our flame of life</i>

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:10.500
<i>Hey, my friends, what scenery do you suppose</i>

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:16.200
<i>awaits us on the other side of this hill?</i>

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:20.810
<i>Hey, my friends, let's climb it together</i>

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:26.630
<i>It's too soon for us to turn back now</i>

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:32.030
<i>The time has come to combine
 together the power dwelling inside me</i>

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:37.310
<i>Gotta release my Soul Drive</i>

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:43.270
<i>Advance, advance, beyond the limits of your strength</i>

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:48.680
<i>Come along with me and burn our flame of life</i>

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:53.850
<i>Keep running, keep running, until you get there</i>

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:59.290
<i>Once again, once again, keep those challenges coming</i>

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:05.680
<i>My friends, keep on living in the here and now</i>

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:11.550
<i>Keep pressing onward together no matter what happens</i>

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:14.810
My turn, draw!

00:04:15.610 --> 00:04:19.360
From my hand I activate the magic card Cards of Sealed Spells!

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:21.360
Numbers 73: The Illusive Grand Clash!

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:21.360
Double Hope vs Double Galaxy-Eyes!

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:23.570
In exchange for sealing the activation of other magic cards this turn,

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:26.240
I can draw 2 cards!

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:28.160
<i>Yes, its there!</i>

00:04:28.830 --> 00:04:30.950
I summon Gagaga Kaiser!

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:39.590
Then, when there is a Gagaga-monster on my field,

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.590
Gagaga Clerk can be special summoned!

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:49.600
Then I activate the effect of Gagaga Kaiser!

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:53.600
Once per turn, I can ban one Monster from my graveyard,

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:58.730
then the LV of all monsters on my field become the same LV as the banned one!

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:01.980
I'll ban Ganbara Knight from my graveyard!

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:04.280
Ganbara Knight's LV is 4!

00:05:04.650 --> 00:05:08.660
Thus, the levels of Gagaga Kaiser and Gagaga Clerk are 4!

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:11.950
There are 2 LV 4 monsters now!

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:13.580
A chance~<i>ura</i>!

00:05:13.870 --> 00:05:15.250
<i>Catto</i> bring it!

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.170
Go, Yuma!

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:22.260
I overlay the LV 4 Gagaga Kaiser and Gagaga Clerk!

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:26.260
With these 2 monsters I build the overlay network!

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:28.260
Xyz summon!

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:33.720
Come forth, Heroic Champion Excalibur!

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:40.730
Oh, isn't that the monster I gave him?!

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:42.730
Pack a punch, Yuma!

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.860
Gauche! Which side are you on?

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:49.700
With Excalibur I'll attack Paladius!

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:52.080
But the ATK of them both is...

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:53.700
... it's both 2000~<i>ura</i>!

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.660
The monster effect of Excalibur activates!

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:02.420
By detaching all overlay units, until the end of the battle, his attack is doubled!

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:05.380
4000 ATK!

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:08.090
Go, Excalibur!

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:12.140
One Slash In Half, Sure-Kill Divine Sword!

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:19.150
Kaito!

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:20.520
Kaito~<i>sama</i>!

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.780
When Paladius was destroyed,

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.490
I can draw 1 card!

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.910
With this I end my turn!

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:36.290
Kaito...

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:38.250
That was amazing~<i>ura</i>.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:39.290
Yes.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:40.830
What a tough duel.

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:44.460
My voice is purring without having a sore throat.

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:46.920
But they are having fun.

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:47.920
Oh?

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:52.090
I think, Yuma and Kaito as well are really enjoying it.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:00.190
Brother is smiling.

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:04.110
He is happy from the bottom of his heart.

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:10.860
<i>Kazuma, does this mean that your son will help Kaito?</i>

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:16.990
Here I go! My turn, draw!

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:20.750
I activate the equip magic Galaxy Zero!

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:24.500
The effects of Galaxy-Eyes in my graveyard are negated,

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:28.920
and equipped with this card it is revived in ATK position!

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:31.430
Be revived, Galaxy-Eyes!

00:07:35.350 --> 00:07:36.600
Galaxy-Eyes!

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:38.720
That's how you do it!

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:41.730
Due to the effect of Galaxy Zero,

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:45.520
it loses 800 ATK during battle!

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:51.400
Even so, Galaxy-Eyes still has the higher ATK!

00:07:51.490 --> 00:07:53.160
Kaito! Go!

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:56.740
Galaxy-Eyes! Attack on Excalibur!

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:00.040
Photon Stream of Destruction!

00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:07.130
Yuma!

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:15.970
Then Galaxy-Eyes ATK returns to normal.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.520
I set one card and end my turn.

00:08:21.230 --> 00:08:22.270
Shoot...

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:27.190
It's not over! I still can go on, Kaito!

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:29.570
Do as you wish.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:35.990
My turn, draw!

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:39.490
I activate the magic card Gagaga Draw!

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.120
From my graveyard, I ban 3 Gagaga monsters...

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.420
... to draw 2 cards.

00:08:53.590 --> 00:08:56.510
Then I activate the equip magic Xyz Revival.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:00.100
I select one Xyz monster from my graveyard,

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:03.980
and special summon it equipped with this card!

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:06.350
Come on, show me all you've got.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:08.690
I will crush all of it!

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:10.780
Exactly my words!

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:13.110
I target Aspiring Emperor Hope.

00:09:13.530 --> 00:09:16.030
Come forth, Aspiring Emperor Hope!

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:25.000
But it falls short to Galaxy-Eyes.

00:09:25.830 --> 00:09:27.170
We'll see if it falls short!

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:30.040
<i>Kattobingu da, ore!</i>

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:32.590
Chaos Xyz Change!

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:35.420
The messenger who changes Chaos into Light!

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:39.050
Come forth, CN 39!

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:42.100
Aspiring Emperor Hope Ray!

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:54.400
<i>Hope Ray... Hope...<i></i></i>

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:55.530
Hu?

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.740
Astral, you said this.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:01.530
That I don't need to be tied to the past anymore.

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:02.910
Yes.

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:06.620
My duel was the duel of a vow.

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:08.250
Vow?

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:13.340
As I vowed to safe Haruto by all means, I had to duel.

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:15.050
Brother...

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:17.760
But... from now on...

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:22.260
Wishes... Hope...

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:25.850
I will duel for myself.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:29.650
That's right, Kaito! Our future belongs to us!

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:32.400
It's us who decide it.

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:44.580
Kaito.

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:48.290
Brother... Me too.

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.630
Now, come at me, Yuma!

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:53.670
Here I go, Kaito!

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:56.300
Hope Ray's effect activates.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:58.970
By detaching 1 overlay unit,

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:03.390
for this turn, Hope Ray's ATK will go up by 500 points.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.350
Overlay Charge!

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:16.400
Then the ATK of one opposing monster will be decreased by 1000 points.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:21.910
Go, Hope Ray, attack Galaxy-Eyes!

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:24.910
Hope Sword Chaos Slash!

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:34.710
I activate the effect of the equip magic Galaxy Zero!

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:41.180
When this card is sent to the graveyard, the destruction of Galaxy-Eyes is negated.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:47.260
But you received the battle damage.

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:48.600
This is...

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:55.940
Wh... why?

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:59.860
The Galaxy Zero I sent to the graveyard has another effect.

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:05.280
When this card leaves the field, the ATK of the monster it equipped changes to Zero.

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:10.200
Yuma, it's the effect of Zerozelock.

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:17.210
I see. Damn!

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:21.010
Zerozelock... Your continuous magic.

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:25.260
Monsters with an ATK of 0 can not be attacked.

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:28.720
Therefore, Hope Ray's attack has been negated.

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:30.390
That means...

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:31.100
Right.

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:35.350
The effect of my continuous magic Battle Gravity will bury you.

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:40.320
When a player who controls a monster did not declare an attack,

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:43.530
that player receives 1000 points of damage!

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.200
Bad!

00:12:45.240 --> 00:12:45.780
Yuma.

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:49.540
Sure! The continuous trap Dimension Gate activates!

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:53.370
It banishes one monster on our field.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:03.550
Since I don't control a monster anymore, the effect damage of Battle Gravity is negated!

00:13:06.300 --> 00:13:08.100
Both of them are in a pretty good mood!

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:10.430
Kaito...

00:13:11.270 --> 00:13:14.020
Kaito~<i>sama</i>, do not lose to that dork!

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.810
Awesome! What a duel this is...

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:19.150
Both of them keep on moving forward,

00:13:20.020 --> 00:13:22.360
towards the hope lying ahead...

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:26.490
I set one card and end my turn.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:29.240
Yuma.

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:29.990
Hu?

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:33.500
You <i>have</i> become stronger.

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:35.580
Wha... what do you mean?

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:39.420
Your spirit of the <i>Kattobingu</i> is really great.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:41.800
You, on your own, already can...

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:43.590
What are you saying!

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:46.630
It's the two of us together that make the <i>Kattobingu</i>.

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:52.220
Let's advance together, forever.

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:55.890
Yuma, let's win.

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:57.390
Sure!

00:13:58.520 --> 00:13:59.980
Yuma, Astral.

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:04.070
Victory will be taken by me in this duel.

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:07.530
My turn!

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:10.660
Draw!

00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:13.620
I summon Galaxy Wizard.

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:24.920
Then Galaxy Wizard's LV increases by 4,

00:14:25.300 --> 00:14:27.970
and he is treated as two Xyz-materials.

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:31.930
Is it coming?

00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:37.520
I overlay the LV 8 Galaxy-Eyes and the Galaxy Wizard counting as 2!

00:14:40.690 --> 00:14:43.980
With these 3 monsters I build the overlay network.

00:14:44.530 --> 00:14:45.610
Xyz summon!

00:14:48.240 --> 00:14:49.450
Great Galaxy of Reversal!

00:14:49.990 --> 00:14:54.030
Become the rolling waves of light and show your mighty form!

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:08.920
Descend, my very soul!

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:12.340
Neo Galaxy-Eyes Photon Dragon!

00:15:16.890 --> 00:15:20.440
However, because it was summoned with the effect of Galaxy Wizard,

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:23.980
Neo Galaxy-Eyes loses 2000 ATK.

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:26.900
But this should be enough.

00:15:27.230 --> 00:15:29.110
Your life is just 300!

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:34.580
Neo Galaxy-Eyes, direct attack!

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:37.660
Ultimate Photon Stream!

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:44.330
With this, Brother wins!

00:15:44.840 --> 00:15:45.340
Yuma!

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:50.010
The effect of the continuous trap Dimension Gate reactivates!

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:54.010
When I receive a direct attack, I can send this card to the graveyard,

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:58.930
to special summon the banned monster with its effects negated!

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:01.600
Revive! Hope Ray!

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:11.860
Hope Ray and Neo Galaxy-Eyes have the same ATK!

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:13.570
So it's a draw!

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:24.420
Go, Yuma!

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:28.840
Alright <i>Kattobingu da, ore</i>!

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:32.300
Quick spell Xyz Double Back activate!

00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:37.970
When an Xyz monster is destroyed and I no longer have a monster on the field,

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:43.890
then the destroyed monster and one with equal or less ATK...

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:46.310
...can be special summoned from the graveyard!

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:47.310
What?

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:49.650
Descend, you two!

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:55.570
Come forth! Aspiring Emperor Hope! Hope Ray!

00:17:09.590 --> 00:17:10.800
Good job, Yuma!

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:12.090
Yuma, you are awesome!

00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:13.920
Is this the decision?

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:14.930
Kaito...

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:18.680
Amazing! Hope and Hope Ray side by side!

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:23.350
Now, in the next turn...

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:26.020
Yes, then the victory will be ours!

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:30.610
What?!

00:17:51.840 --> 00:17:54.590
That is... 
I can't believe it!

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:57.630
Xyz Double Back!

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:02.560
You have the same card as me?!

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:05.100
You did it, Kaito~<i>sama</i>!

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:07.060
Stupid dork!

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:10.860
When compared, <i>Kaitobingu</i> is much better than <i>Kattobingu</i>!

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:12.020
Kaito...

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:14.940
Yuma... Astral...

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:22.780
Galaxy-Eyes and Neo Galaxy-Eyes together, attack Hope and Hope Ray!

00:18:23.790 --> 00:18:26.410
Photon Stream of Destruction!

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:32.170
Go! Ultimate Photon Stream!

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:20.970
It... hurts...

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:23.010
Oh dear, so I lost.

00:19:30.230 --> 00:19:30.890
Kaito...

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:39.860
Kaito...

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:43.910
Next time, I will absolutely beat you.

00:19:44.780 --> 00:19:46.450
I'll be your opponent again.

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:47.990
As often as you like.

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:54.460
Yes, and I'll gonna make it!

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:56.750
As long as I don't give up and keep on <i>kattobing</i>ing...

00:19:57.130 --> 00:20:00.300
... one day, maybe I'll surpass you!

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:11.020
Yuma!

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.230
Yuma!
Yuma~<i>kun</i>!

00:20:15.770 --> 00:20:16.860
Kotori...

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:21.070
Yuma?

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:22.320
Yuma!

00:20:22.740 --> 00:20:23.490
Yuma!

00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:24.610
Hey, Yuma!

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:26.070
Yuma!

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:27.280
Yuma!

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:28.540
Yuma~<i>kun</i>!

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:29.540
Oh?

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:41.880
Brother... Yuma... Thank you.

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:49.770
That was some good mood!

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:52.430
Yuma, see ya.

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:02.110
Yuma, Astral...

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:09.410
Yuma... Yuma, oh geez...

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:11.200
Sound sleep~<i>ura</i>.

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:17.380
In conclusion... ... it's so typically Yuma.

00:21:17.540 --> 00:21:20.670
How about letting him sleep on my lap!

00:21:21.130 --> 00:21:23.050
Hey Astral, make Yuma...

00:21:24.090 --> 00:21:26.550
There is nothing even I can do.

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:29.260
Hm <i>Kattobingu da</i> zzz...

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:32.850
Can't be helped then.

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:35.140
Just let him be for a bit.

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:38.020
<i>Observation #21:</i>

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:42.650
<i>Apparently it seems like one can feel good about a loss as well.</i>

00:21:44.440 --> 00:21:49.870
<i>We stand tall, until we have victory in our grasp</i>

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:55.250
<i>Move on ahead, speeding up our throbbing beats</i>

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:06.050
<i>Listen boys and girls, here's the secret to boys and girls like you</i>

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:10.140
<i>You're really just so spontaneous, wild as can be</i>

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:11.510
<i>I bet you didn't know?</i>

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:14.180
<i>You might be a handful, but what's wrong with that?</i>

00:22:14.350 --> 00:22:16.810
<i>Be up to no good, but learn for real</i>

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:22.020
<i>Go the unpredictable route and shuffle your cards with a goal in mind</i>

00:22:22.190 --> 00:22:27.360
<i>Whenever you feel like you've lost your way, just take a minute to close your eyes...</i>

00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:32.990
<i>Shout "stop!" with all you've got, and there's your boundary line.</i>

00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:39.500
<i>We stand tall, until we have victory in our grasp</i>

00:22:39.750 --> 00:22:45.130
<i>We won't just stop here, not when we don't want to have any regrets.</i>

00:22:45.130 --> 00:22:50.260
<i>Even if we get hurt, we can't just hesitate now</i>

00:22:50.510 --> 00:22:55.930
<i>We won't just give up, not when our future's a lot brighter than our today</i>

00:22:55.930 --> 00:23:01.270
<i>Seriousness... It'll only make us keep fighting even harder</i>

00:23:01.310 --> 00:23:06.740
<i>We'll always get as fascinated as we want, and we'll fight on every day</i>

00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:28.590
Tsukumo Yuma, Astral.

00:23:29.630 --> 00:23:31.260
I did not expect this.

00:23:34.850 --> 00:23:37.680
Next time we may have to get out ourselves.

00:23:41.560 --> 00:23:44.690
Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal will get a power up!

00:23:45.400 --> 00:23:48.990
Wha-wha-what, it's Yu-Gi-Oh! Zexal 'second'!

00:23:49.650 --> 00:23:53.070
which is about the new foes from Barian World,

00:23:53.410 --> 00:23:56.200
who Rank-up the Xyz Monsters!

00:23:56.450 --> 00:23:58.370
Just what is going on?

00:23:59.540 --> 00:24:05.420
Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II broadcast starts October 7th, 5:30 PM

00:24:06.960 --> 00:24:08.460
You absolutely gotta watch it!
